Read CLAUDE.md.

Implement Sprint 1.1: the CRM entity model and API. Do NOT build UI yet.

Entities (each in its own internal module with repository, service, handler):
- Account (exists — extend with: industry text, employee_count int,
  website text, owner_id uuid)
- Contact (first_name, last_name, email citext, phone text, title text,
  account_id uuid FK, owner_id uuid, do_not_contact bool, consent_status
  text CHECK IN ('none','granted','revoked'), consent_source text,
  consent_captured_at timestamptz)
- Opportunity (name, account_id uuid FK, pipeline_id uuid FK, stage_id uuid
  FK, amount_cents bigint, currency text DEFAULT 'USD', close_date date,
  owner_id uuid, status text CHECK IN ('open','won','lost'))
- Pipeline (name, is_default bool) — one per tenant
- Stage (pipeline_id, name, ordinal int, is_closed_won bool,
  is_closed_lost bool)
- Activity (type text CHECK IN ('note','email_sent','email_received',
  'call','meeting','task'), subject text, body text, occurred_at
  timestamptz, contact_id uuid NULL, opportunity_id uuid NULL,
  account_id uuid NOT NULL, metadata jsonb)

All tables: ENABLE + FORCE RLS, tenant_id column, RLS policy via
current_tenant(), indexes prefixed with tenant_id, updated_at trigger.
Add a `record_event` helper that appends to outbox inside the caller's tx:
contact.created, contact.updated, opportunity.created,
opportunity.stage_changed, activity.logged.

Deliverables:
- One migration per entity (or one migration with all — your call, but
  reversible).
- internal/{account,contact,opportunity,pipeline,activity}/ with repo +
  service + handler.
- REST endpoints under /api/v1: standard CRUD, list with pagination
  (cursor-based, tenant-scoped), filter by owner_id and status.
- GraphQL read layer for account-360: account + contacts + open
  opportunities + last 20 activities, single query.
- 10+ tests per module: tenant isolation (assert a contact created under
  tenant A is invisible under tenant B), RLS WITH CHECK rejects cross-
  tenant insert, event emitted exactly once on create/update, pagination
  cursor does not leak across tenants.

Acceptance criteria:
- `make test` green with all new tests.
- Cross-tenant read AND write both rejected.
- Events appear on Kafka with the correct tenant_id in headers.
- No repository method has `WHERE tenant_id` — RLS supplies it. If you
  find yourself adding one, stop and flag it.

Commit when green.